# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Secrets / local env (never commit API keys)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# local/session state
.omc/
*.log
nohup.out
.pytest_cache/

# Reproduction run logs are a durable, git-tracked record (docs/14): un-ignore
# them despite the global *.log above so nothing from a run is volatile.
!results/repro/logs/
!results/repro/logs/*.log

# Heavy run artifacts (docs/14 §Artifacts): the full LLM I/O trace and the
# per-item memory snapshot can be very large on full runs, and the persisted
# stores are binary DB dirs. They are DURABLE on disk (never deleted, so nothing
# is lost) but NOT git-committed, to avoid repo bloat. The summary `.json` — the
# artifact every published number is read from — IS committed and is not matched
# here.
results/repro/*.llm-trace.jsonl
results/repro/*.memory.jsonl
results/repro/stores/

# The evolution-log dump joins them for the same reason. It carries the full
# payload of every op, so it duplicates the snapshot's content and grows with
# the run (12MB for one 10-conversation arm). The NUMBERS the op-structure
# claims are actually read from — the `op_counts` block, keyed "OP:target_type"
# — live in the committed summary JSON, so nothing citable depends on this file
# being in git.
results/repro/*.ops.jsonl

# Per-question `.records.jsonl` joined this list on 2026-08-04. It used to be
# committed as a "small" artifact and the eight A-Mem-campaign files still are —
# tracked files are unaffected by a new ignore rule, and un-committing them would
# rewrite history for no gain. But "small" stopped being true: A-Mem's are ~19MB
# each while Track 1 Nemori's are ~46MB, and committing that track's six would
# have taken the repo from 141MB to over 400MB with a per-track increment after
# it. Same standing rule as the traces above — durable on disk, not in git.
results/repro/*.records.jsonl

# Set-aside copies from re-runs (`mv artifact artifact.rewriteon` before letting
# a run overwrite it, `.partialN` for a superseded attempt). Hand-made, not
# harness-produced; they are prior editions of the artifacts above, kept on disk
# under the same never-delete rule.
results/repro/*.rewriteon
results/repro/*.partial[0-9]

# Internal planning docs (specs/plans/handoffs) stay local; history keeps the old ones.
docs/_internal/
